   "text": "I read the molecule as a macrocyclic ester built from these pieces, then assigned each stereocentre against the (S) labels in the drawing.\n\n- **Macrocycle core:** a piperazic acid (hexahydropyridazine-3-carboxylic acid, S) whose carboxyl group is esterified by a neopentyl-type alcohol, \u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013CH2\u2013. That CH2 is attached to C3 of the indole.\n- **Indole:** N-ethyl, with C2 bearing a pyridin-3-yl group. The pyridine C2 carries an (S)-CH(CH3)OCH3. Indole C5 is joined to a phenyl ring at a meta position.\n- **Phenyl linker:** the other meta position carries CH2\u2013CH(NH\u2013)\u2013C(=O)\u2013, an (S) phenylalanine-like unit whose C=O acylates the free piperazic N1.\n- **Side chain:** the \u03b1-NH is acylated by N-methyl-(S)-valine. Its N-methyl nitrogen is acylated by 4-fluoropiperidine-4-carbonyl. The piperidine nitrogen carries the (E)-4-(dimethylamino)but-2-enoyl group, C(=O)\u2013CH=CH\u2013CH2\u2013N(CH3)2.\n\nFor each stereocentre I worked out the CIP priorities and matched the SMILES @/@@ to the drawn (S) labels. This gave `[C@@H]` for the piperazic carbon and `[C@H]` for the phenylalanine \u03b1-carbon, the valine \u03b1-carbon and the methoxyethyl carbon. The enamide is written as trans (`/C=C/`).\n\nSMILES: O=C1OCC(C)(C)Cc2c(-c3cccnc3[C@H](C)OC)n(CC)c3ccc(cc23)-c4cccc(c4)C[C@H](NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)C)N(C)C(=O)C6(F)CCN(CC6)C(=O)/C=C/CN(C)C)C(=O)N5CCC[C@@H]1N5"
  }
